WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.520
Three children, age 5 to 11, and a teacher were killed at a bend Oregon school. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 24. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Ben Poli set a 16-year-old boy from the city carried out the attack at Silver Rail Elementary on Thursday afternoon, and a community member chased him inside and shot him dead, the BBC reported. Police chief Mike Krantz said the attacker has not been publicly identified, and that he got through the doors by firing at the locks.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.280
Police said it is unclear whether he had any connection to the school.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.080
A seven-year-old and a 54-year-old teacher were taken to hospital in critical condition.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.700
The first call reached police at 1259 local time,

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.480
from someone who said an unknown person was shooting a long gun into a car.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.400
Pictures released from the scene show a red truck punched with bullet holes.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.780
Minutes later, county dispatch took emergency calls that he had gone into the school.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.600
Officers arrived three minutes after the bystander shot him, confirmed he was dead

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.060
and searched the building. Oregon Governor Tina Cotec praised that bystander, saying the person

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.360
had stepped in heroically, and she told them the actions carry a heavy emotional burden,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.960
and that her thoughts were with them. Steven Cook, the school district's top administrative

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.940
official, said the community was stunned and heartbroken, and that words could not carry the grief.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:24.640
About 450 children attend Silver Rail, with more than 40 adults on staff, and Ben schools are closed

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.560
on Friday so people can have time to heal. Children went by bus to a nearby church used

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.780
as a reunification center, and some parents brought stuffed animals and other comfort

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:39.640
items from home. Teacher Kathy Sheel Smith told KPTV she tried to keep children calm after

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.720
she saw the gunman approach, that some were praying and some were comforting one another,

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.380
and that she was sure every teacher thought that day might be the day they would die.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.440
Reporter Michael Cohn said the school was locked down, that students reached parents outside

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.220
on Apple Watches, and that parents stood stunned at what he called a neighborhood school in a mountain

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:03.100
town. Local media said the school got classroom doors in 2022 that lock with the flip of a switch.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:10.380
A school shooting database counted 235 incidents at American schools last year, and at least 140 so far

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:16.480
this year. A person under 18 cannot buy a firearm in Oregon. The state lets a juvenile possess one

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.760
with a parent's permission, and only for certain uses such as hunting. Officials would not say what

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.240
type of weapon was used or how many rounds were fired.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.760
